Network running at a decent time so we can train today's

00:36:33.690 --> 00:36:36.710
kids, cause it's, it, it, the stories are still, you know

00:36:36.730 --> 00:36:37.730
they're timeless.

00:36:37.730 --> 00:36:44.529
&gt;&gt;audience4: They are. So, as you mentioned--

00:36:44.549 --> 00:36:45.549
[laughter]

00:36:44.549 --> 00:36:49.130
So, as you mentioned earlier, there's a lot of energy effort

00:36:49.150 --> 00:36:52.150
being expended to deal with the symptoms of environmental

00:36:52.170 --> 00:36:58.079
problems, and of the 2.4 trillion dollars that our federal

00:36:58.099 --> 00:37:03.529
government collects in taxes, 95 percent of that comes from

00:37:03.549 --> 00:37:07.949
taxing wealth, innovation, labor, and less than five percent

00:37:07.969 --> 00:37:11.440
of that comes from taxing activities that generate negative

00:37:11.460 --> 00:37:14.589
actionalities; pollution, resource depletion, waste and

00:37:14.609 --> 00:37:15.609
inefficiency.

00:37:15.609 --> 00:37:20.509
So, my question, what do you see is like, as the best way to

00:37:20.529 --> 00:37:24.659
actually address the root cause of environmental problems,

00:37:24.679 --> 00:37:27.299
instead of just dealing with the symptoms. I know you

00:37:27.319 --> 00:37:31.009
mentioned earlier population control, have any ideas?

00:37:31.029 --> 00:37:33.420
&gt;&gt;Ted: Not population control; family planning.

00:37:33.440 --> 00:37:34.440
&gt;&gt;audience4: Family planning.

00:37:34.440 --> 00:37:36.440
&gt;&gt;Ted: People don't like to be controlled--

00:37:35.690 --> 00:37:36.690
&gt;&gt;audience4: Ok,

00:37:36.690 --> 00:37:38.190
&gt;&gt;Ted: but they like to plan.

00:37:38.190 --> 00:37:41.079
&gt;&gt;audience4: All right.

00:37:41.099 --> 00:37:42.099
[laughs] Population planning, then?

00:37:42.089 --> 00:37:43.089
[laughter]

00:37:42.089 --> 00:37:45.589
&gt;&gt;Ted: It, it, it's very important and that's why I, I, I

00:37:45.589 --> 00:37:49.420
forbade the, the TV announcers on CNN to use the word "

00:37:49.440 --> 00:37:52.190
foreign" because it was, CNN was going all over the world,

00:37:51.980 --> 00:37:54.989
they looked really stupid. Foreign, who's foreign? Everybody

00:37:55.009 --> 00:37:57.860
was close together now because we interconnected the whole

00:37:57.880 --> 00:38:03.789
world. So, but what's, what's the question?

00:38:03.809 --> 00:38:04.809
[laughter]

00:38:03.809 --> 00:38:05.059
&gt;&gt;audience4: So, what do you--

00:38:05.059 --> 00:38:06.559
&gt;&gt;Ted: That was a long question.

00:38:06.559 --> 00:38:09.309
&gt;&gt;audience4: How, how, what are some ways in which we can

00:38:09.309 --> 00:38:11.809
deal with the root cause of environmental problems? What do

00:38:11.809 --> 00:38:13.559
you see as the most effective ways?

00:38:13.559 --> 00:38:15.559
&gt;&gt;Jason: Should we be, for example. taxing polluters?

00:38:15.559 --> 00:38:19.480
&gt;&gt;Ted: Ta-, taxing pollu-, absolutely. Tax the polluters,

00:38:19.500 --> 00:38:23.489
you bet. And then, we made the-, absolutely. That's who

00:38:23.509 --> 00:38:26.920
should be paying for it. That's who, you know, why should we

00:38:26.940 --> 00:38:30.289
be paying for somebody else?s pollution? That's not the

00:38:30.309 --> 00:38:31.309
solution.

00:38:31.309 --> 00:38:34.429
&gt;&gt;audience4: And if I could follow up, what do you see as

00:38:34.449 --> 00:38:36.409
the role of education versus technology--

00:38:36.429 --> 00:38:38.630
&gt;&gt;Ted: Tax gasoline. You know.

00:38:38.650 --> 00:38:43.639
&gt;&gt;Jason: And he's also asking do you see education playing a

00:38:43.659 --> 00:38:45.799
role in this as well?

00:38:45.819 --> 00:38:48.319
&gt;&gt;Ted: Of course. Everything plays a role in it. Captain

00:38:48.319 --> 00:38:50.909
Planet was television, but it was educational television,

00:38:50.929 --> 00:38:51.929
right?

00:38:51.929 --> 00:38:52.929
[audience chatter]

00:38:52.329 --> 00:38:55.639
Sure, education's extremely important. If we don't have a

00:38:55.659 --> 00:38:59.849
good educational system that teaches, Ger-, Germany had a

00:38:59.869 --> 00:39:04.159
great educational system in 1935. The only problem was it

00:39:04.179 --> 00:39:05.269
was preaching hatred.

00:39:05.289 --> 00:39:09.849
You know, it, it was saying that, the educational system was

00:39:09.869 --> 00:39:14.210
anti-Semitic there. But the, but what we need an education

00:39:14.230 --> 00:39:19.230
system that's strongly educates us about the environment and

00:39:19.250 --> 00:39:22.500
how important it is to preserve it. You bet. It's not just

00:39:22.210 --> 00:39:26.119
something that we just can, can rape and pillage and, and,

00:39:26.139 --> 00:39:28.889
and, and, and expect it to support us.

00:39:28.909 --> 00:39:32.409
I, I wanna see us sustainable. I'd like to see, what's wrong

00:39:32.210 --> 00:39:35.029
with a concept of where five thousand years from now people

00:39:35.049 --> 00:39:39.650
are still here? Living in harmony with nature, right? And

00:39:39.670 --> 00:39:43.239
having a great life. I, I think what we've done, one of the

00:39:43.259 --> 00:39:46.009
biggest mistakes we've made in America and in the Western

00:39:45.759 --> 00:39:49.400
world to a smaller degree, but America is, is we emphasize

00:39:49.420 --> 00:39:54.319
that how much money you have and how much you spend is what

00:39:54.339 --> 00:39:56.819
determines how happy you are. That?s not right.

00:39:56.839 --> 00:39:59.250
The thing that really determines your happiness is your

00:39:59.269 --> 00:40:03.569
relationships. with you family, with your friends. And, and

00:40:03.589 --> 00:40:07.219
we need to have, we need to change over, that's what got us

00:40:07.239 --> 00:40:10.309
in all this financial problem. People wanted to spend more

00:40:10.329 --> 00:40:12.909
money so they borrowed, went out and borrowed more than

00:40:12.929 --> 00:40:14.869
their house was worth against their house.

00:40:14.889 --> 00:40:17.639
The banks lent them the money; that was the banks mistake.

00:40:17.630 --> 00:40:21.130
We were all, but it's our fault that, that we got in this

00:40:21.139 --> 00:40:25.440
problem. Basically, it was because we were spending more,

00:40:25.460 --> 00:40:29.099
George Soros figured it out, I think six percent a year for

00:40:29.119 --> 00:40:32.739
five, the last five years, we spent more than, than we were

00:40:32.759 --> 00:40:35.539
earning. And borrowing the money from the Chinese, we can't

00:40:35.559 --> 00:40:36.759
operate like that.

00:40:36.779 --> 00:40:39.529
What we should do is live in smaller houses; they're

00:40:38.980 --> 00:40:43.480
building smaller houses now. Smaller houses and smaller

00:40:43.500 --> 00:40:46.500
automobiles; I drive a Prius. That's my main car, you know,

00:40:46.480 --> 00:40:49.730
and I'm a billionaire still. And, and I don't have a

00:40:49.699 --> 00:40:53.199
gigantic house, I got a nice house, I'll tell ya, I do, I

00:40:52.659 --> 00:40:53.659
do.

00:40:53.659 --> 00:40:54.659
[laughter]

00:40:53.659 --> 00:40:59.639
But it's not gigantic. I mean, you know, I don't feel guilty

00:40:59.659 --> 00:41:04.650
about living there and, and, and, and, and, and put more

00:41:04.670 --> 00:41:07.489
emphasis, get to know your next door neighbors. Don't drive

00:41:07.509 --> 00:41:10.509
all the way across town. But, get to know the people next

00:41:10.519 --> 00:41:13.519
door. Then play bridge with them, you know? It doesn't cost

00:41:13.440 --> 00:41:17.719
anything, for Christ's sake, you know, cook dinner together.

00:41:17.739 --> 00:41:21.239
You have more fun than you do if you go out and drink too

00:41:21.239 --> 00:41:23.989
much at some fancy restaurant anyway. And I'm in the

00:41:23.739 --> 00:41:26.239
restaurant business, so please go out to the, the moderately

00:41:25.739 --> 00:41:26.739
priced restaurants.

00:41:26.739 --> 00:41:27.739
[laughter]

00:41:26.739 --> 00:41:29.839
Like Ted's Montana Grill, we're not in California yet.

00:41:29.859 --> 00:41:34.539
Anyway, does that answer the question? That's a, you guys

00:41:34.559 --> 00:41:37.309
are asking me, you guys and girls are asking me tough

00:41:36.440 --> 00:41:37.440
questions.

00:41:37.440 --> 00:41:38.440
[laughter]

