&gt;&gt;Ted: Well, it depends on how its, how it's used. Cause if

00:42:00.380 --> 00:42:05.940
it's used to turn people against the government, it's got,

00:42:05.960 --> 00:42:10.630
my concept of, of a way I try to run CNN was to tell the

00:42:10.650 --> 00:42:17.699
truth in a non-, a non-threatening way and to, when,

00:42:17.719 --> 00:42:20.589
whenever there were controversial issues, to seek out the

00:42:20.609 --> 00:42:24.429
leading proponents of both sides and let them air in their

00:42:24.449 --> 00:42:28.259
opinions and let the viewers make up their own minds. Some,

00:42:28.279 --> 00:42:32.599
some of this talk radio now tries to make up, it, your mind

00:42:32.619 --> 00:42:36.309
for you and to convince you that they're right, and you

00:42:36.329 --> 00:42:41.659
know, they're right wing whatever. Or left wing. But, but

00:42:41.679 --> 00:42:44.429
that's the way, the way I try to do it.

00:42:43.679 --> 00:42:48.519
It's very complicated, it's, these are not, your, your, you'

00:42:48.539 --> 00:42:52.809
d expect Stanford Business School, post graduate, you expect

00:42:52.829 --> 00:42:55.860
good questions and tha-, we're getting them. They're most

00:42:55.880 --> 00:42:59.769
complicated questions that, that you could ask. But that's

00:42:59.789 --> 00:43:03.309
ok. I, I just wish I could answer them better, but the

00:43:03.329 --> 00:43:07.739
answers can't be simple, they have to be com-, they're,

00:43:07.759 --> 00:43:11.719
they're complex by their very nature. Complex answers to

00:43:11.739 --> 00:43:13.369
complex questions.

